findings.body:
Removing `@require_role("admin")` leaves `delete_user` with no access control. Any client that can hit `DELETE /users/<user>` can remove arbitrary accounts (`USERS.remove(user)`) and get `204`.

Cleanup jobs that need delete access should authenticate as a principal that is explicitly allowed to delete (for example a `cleanup`/`admin` role or service account) and keep a server-side authorization check on this route. Do not ship an unauthenticated destructive endpoint.

```suggestion
@require_role("admin")
def delete_user(user):
```
